{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:bd94c3b597a0bf79","name":"Twi'lek Saboteur","source":{"id":"source:reference-bd94c3b597a0bf79","title":"Twi'lek Saboteur","revision":25261,"timestamp":"2024-11-13T20:28:09Z","sha256":"81a3ac625321dab53574c3d02c7e8e70acb2eb39ab705619af61e809b51fc8d3","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=25261","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Twi%27lek%20Saboteur&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-bd94c3b597a0bf79","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Twi'lek Saboteurs specialize in infiltration and subtle sabotage. Being a Twi'lek Saboteur, like being a spy, demands a mixture of skill, dedication, and a willingness to live in the shadows and to embrace secrecy and deception as a way of life. For a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Twi'lek"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Twi%27lek","referenceId":"reference:b787e536e15f2960"}," the key to successful sabotage is the same as the key to all other forms of success- understanding and subtly manipulating people. Ultimately, even the best security can be overridden by a sympathetic guard who decides to make an exception for someone who claims to be late for work and is worried about getting fired or who has forgotten their ID Badge.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["After getting past security, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Twi'lek"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Twi%27lek","referenceId":"reference:b787e536e15f2960"}," either sneaks off and stealthily finds a way to his objective or continues to bluff his way past every obstacle, perhaps pretending to be a repair technician who has been ordered to \"fix\" the very device they are intent upon sabotaging. Twi'lek Saboteurs eschew armor and heavy weaponry, rarely carrying more than a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hold-Out Blaster Pistol"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hold-Out_Blaster_Pistol","referenceId":"reference:99ddc9f0285574f3"},", because they know that having to use heavy weapons or armor means that they have already failed. \n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Twi'lek Saboteur Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The most skilled Twi'lek Saboteurs avoid notice altogether. The other employees in a factory or research lab are unlikely to remember the friendly but easily forgettable ",{"tag":"a","children":["Twi'lek"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Twi%27lek","referenceId":"reference:b787e536e15f2960"}," technician who worked there for a short while. However, these same people will rarely be able to forget the time when their prized weapon or vehicle failed spectacularly during its first major test. In the case of corporate sabotage, the people involved instead remember the time that a piece of new technology catastrophically backfired when the corporation's leaders demonstrated it before the Queen of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Naboo"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Naboo","referenceId":"reference:8c2767dbc8d173d5"},", in an effort to convince her government to purchase it. The only time the presence of a Twi'lek Saboteur becomes obvious is when something goes wrong, such as someone noticing a minor discrepancy between their actions and the person they are impersonating or a Security Droid hearing a soft noise coming from a hallway or storage room that should be empty. At this point, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Twi'lek"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Twi%27lek","referenceId":"reference:b787e536e15f2960"}," will either try to swiftly accomplish their job and flee, or leave quickly and try again another day.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Hiring a Twi'lek Saboteur is often somewhat challenging, since ",{"tag":"a","children":["Twi'leks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Twi%27leks"}," are not inclined to trust others. The Twi'lek Saboteur attempts to find out all they can about a prospective client before accepting any offer of employment, so that they can be certain that their employer will not double-cross them.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Twi'lek Saboteur Statistics (CL 6)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Twi'lek"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Twi%27lek","referenceId":"reference:b787e536e15f2960"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scoundrel"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scoundrel","referenceId":"reference:316d580fd4c35ecc"}," 4/",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldier","referenceId":"reference:f826baa05bef6921"}," 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 4\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +4; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low-Light Vision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low-Light_Vision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +9\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, Ryl, 3 Unassigned\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 19 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 18), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 20, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 18\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":[